---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About" description="Made by a mum, for the world our kids are growing into. The story behind Mini Brains Trust, a future-ready home kindy for Australian 3 to 5 year olds.">
  <main>
    <header class="abouthero">
      <span class="blob" style="width:300px;height:300px;background:var(--pink);opacity:.5;left:-80px;top:0;"></span>
      <span class="blob b2" style="width:220px;height:220px;background:var(--peri);opacity:.3;right:-40px;top:40px;"></span>
      <span class="blob b3" style="width:180px;height:180px;background:var(--yellow);opacity:.55;right:120px;bottom:-30px;"></span>
      <span class="floaticon" style="left:9%;top:150px;transform:rotate(-7deg);animation:float 8s ease-in-out infinite;"><img src="/icons/birds.png" alt="" /></span>
      <span class="floaticon" style="right:10%;bottom:20px;transform:rotate(7deg);animation:float 10s ease-in-out infinite;"><img src="/icons/space.png" alt="" /></span>
      <div class="wrap center">
        <h1>Made by a mum, for the world our kids are growing into.</h1>
        <p class="lead">Mini Brains Trust is a simple way to grow the strengths that matter most, ten minutes of real play at a time. Here is why we made it.</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section>
      <div class="wrap feature">
        <div class="storyvisual">
          <span class="blob" style="width:240px;height:240px;background:var(--paleblue,#CDDBF9);opacity:.7;"></span>
          <div class="iconcluster">
            <span class="ci" style="left:10px;top:10px;transform:rotate(-6deg)"><img src="/icons/space.png" alt="" /></span>
            <span class="ci" style="right:6px;top:50px;transform:rotate(8deg)"><img src="/icons/numbers.png" alt="" /></span>
            <span class="ci" style="left:70px;bottom:8px;transform:rotate(4deg)"><img src="/icons/story.png" alt="" /></span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2>The world has changed what it means to be clever.</h2>
          <p class="lede">For a long time, being clever meant knowing things. That is quietly ending. A machine can recall more than any of us and answer in a heartbeat. So what gives your child an edge is shifting towards the human strengths a screen cannot teach, the very ones it quietly wears away. Those strengths are grown slowly, through play, and ages three to five is when the ground is softest.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="founderblock">
          <div class="fimg"><img src="/bird.png" alt="" /></div>
          <div>
            <h2>Hi, I'm Tina. A mum, and a scrappy outback kid.</h2>
            <p>I grew up in the outback with a lot of space to roam and time to fill. I spent my days building tree houses, constructing underground forts, wandering through bulldozer cuts and finding interesting scraps to transform into a new toy. I learnt to make my own fun by fixing things and working things out for myself. These are the skills that have served me most as an adult. It taught me problem solving, to have a go, to stick at something hard, and to be resourceful when there was no easy answer to reach for.</p>
            <p>These days I work in AI with a background in tech and writing, so I spend my time looking straight at where the world is heading. That is what makes me certain which human skills are worth protecting and nurturing in our little ones, and why I decided not to wait for school to catch up.</p>
            <p>Mini Brains Trust is the good part of a resourceful childhood, made simple for parents who are flat out. Steady, playful practice at being a wonderfully, capably human, with whatever is already around you.</p>
            <p class="sig">Tina, founder and mum</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="wrap center">
        <h2>A brains trust of educators, with an eye on what's next.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Most learning products are made by teachers, or by technologists. This one comes from both, in the one family.</p>
        <div class="creds">
          <div class="credcard">
            <div class="cover" style="background:var(--paleblue,#CDDBF9)"><span class="cblob" style="background:var(--peri);right:18px;bottom:6px;opacity:.4;"></span><img src="/icons/space.png" alt="" /></div>
            <div class="cbody">
              <h3>An AI educator's eye on the future</h3>
              <p>Tina works in AI for a living and comes from a tech background. Watching where technology is heading every day is exactly what tells us which human skills are worth protecting now.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="credcard">
            <div class="cover" style="background:var(--berrytint)"><span class="cblob" style="background:var(--pink);right:18px;bottom:6px;opacity:.5;"></span><img src="/icons/story.png" alt="" /></div>
            <div class="cbody">
              <h3>A family of teachers</h3>
              <p>Tina grew up surrounded by educators: a retired schoolteacher mum, a sister teaching high school, and a sister lecturing at university. Decades of real classroom experience sit behind how this is built.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="credcard">
            <div class="cover" style="background:#E7F3E9"><span class="cblob" style="background:var(--green);right:18px;bottom:6px;opacity:.3;"></span><img src="/icons/feelings.png" alt="" /></div>
            <div class="cbody">
              <h3>A mum, in the thick of it</h3>
              <p>Every idea is built and tested at a real kitchen table, on real three to five year olds, so it holds up when you are flat out and the witching hour hits.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="namebox">That's the <b>trust</b> in Mini Brains Trust: a little brains trust of educators behind every day of play, steered by someone who understands the AI age your child is growing into.</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="wrap center">
        <h2>Eight little strengths, woven through everything.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Every activity is built to grow two or three of these. Problem-solving and critical thinking run all the way through.</p>
        <div class="pillars" style="text-align:left">
          <div class="pill"><div class="dot" style="--c:var(--peri)"></div><h3>Attention</h3><p>Staying with something slow, and the patience that grows from it.</p></div>
          <div class="pill"><div class="dot" style="--c:var(--berry)"></div><h3>Curiosity</h3><p>Asking the next question instead of taking the first answer.</p></div>
          <div class="pill"><div class="dot" style="--c:var(--green)"></div><h3>Real world</h3><p>Hands that know how things actually work.</p></div>
          <div class="pill"><div class="dot" style="--c:var(--pink)"></div><h3>Creativity</h3><p>Making something new that is all their own.</p></div>
          <div class="pill"><div class="dot" style="--c:var(--peach)"></div><h3>Agency</h3><p>Being the one who decides and makes things happen.</p></div>
          <div class="pill"><div class="dot" style="--c:var(--berry)"></div><h3>Connection</h3><p>Reading a real face, sharing a real moment.</p></div>
          <div class="pill"><div class="dot" style="--c:var(--peri)"></div><h3>Discernment</h3><p>Telling what's true from what only sounds true.</p></div>
          <div class="pill"><div class="dot" style="--c:var(--olive)"></div><h3>Sticking at it</h3><p>Staying with something hard until it works.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="wrap center">
        <p class="lede">Wondering how this lines up with big school? See how our play supports <a href="/school-readiness/" style="color:var(--berryink);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;">school readiness across the Australian Curriculum</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="panel lav">
          <h2>Private by design, and always will be.</h2>
          <p class="lede">We collect as little as possible, we never sell it, and there are no ads chasing your child around the internet. What happens at your kitchen table stays there. It is built into how the whole thing works, and it always will be.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="final" id="join">
      <div class="wrap center">
        <h2>Come grow a little human with us.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Join the waitlist for early access, a founding-member price, and a real say in what we build.</p>
        <form class="form" id="waitlist-form" name="waitlist" method="POST" data-netlify="true" netlify-honeypot="bot-field">
          <input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="waitlist" />
          <p hidden><label>Leave empty: <input name="bot-field" /></label></p>
          <div class="row">
            <input type="text" name="first_name" placeholder="Your first name" autocomplete="given-name" />
            <input type="email" name="email" placeholder="Your email" required autocomplete="email" />
          </div>
          <button type="submit" class="btn lg">Join the waitlist &nbsp;&rarr;</button>
        </form>
        <div class="thanks" id="thanks">
          <div class="fred">You're on the list.</div>
          <p>Thanks for backing this early. We'll be in touch before anyone else.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
